{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1133","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1133","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1133\",\"parent_revision\":\"b145195b7a35e02271e291ddb678a25e0117fcf9\",\"root_revision\":\"af462434cf141922c267bb09c6f341b6979311d3abe7358f149790090de8fae2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe add-new-feature workflow Phase 3 (Architecture Spec) resolves the design-spec role via language manifests. When no language manifest matches, it falls back to general-purpose. A general-purpose agent lacks the skills, permissions, input/output patterns, quality standards, and design minimums required by the development harness. It has no knowledge of the Component Design and Verification Contract formats consumed by swarm-task-planner.\\n\\nResult: architecture output at unpredictable quality \u2014 as observed in session 2026-03-30 when Phase 3 was delegated to general-purpose for a skill-file change (SKILL.md, agent files, docs), where the language manifest's python-cli-design-spec role did not apply.\\n\\nWhat is needed: a harness-level baseline architect agent that:\\n1. Applies general software architecture best practices regardless of language or file type (skill files, agent files, markdown docs, config, Python, TypeScript)\\n2. Produces output in the Component Design and Verification Contract formats required by swarm-task-planner\\n3. Knows the development harness artifact conventions (architect-{slug}.md, state-relative paths, artifact_register pattern)\\n4. Is used as the design-spec role fallback when no language-specific agent applies\\n5. Includes quality gates equivalent to those in python-cli-design-spec.md but language-agnostic\\n\\nReference agents to learn from:\\n- plugins/python-engineering/agents/python-cli-design-spec.md (language-specific design spec)\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md (consumes architect spec output)\\n\\nWithout this agent, Phase 3 of add-new-feature produces inconsistent architecture quality for all non-Python changes: skill file changes, agent file changes, documentation-first features, and cross-language changes all fall through to general-purpose.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **create baseline harness-agnostic architect agent for swarm-task-planner compatibility** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed gap \u2014 session 2026-03-30, /dh:work-backlog-item anti-loop, Phase 3 fallback to general-purpose for SKILL.md change\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-30\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n**Affected path**: `add-new-feature` workflow Phase 3 (Architecture Spec) for all non-Python changes.\\n\\nEvery skill file change, agent file change, documentation-first feature, TypeScript change, and cross-language refactor that goes through the harness currently falls through to general-purpose when no language manifest matches. The quality of Phase 3 output is then non-deterministic \u2014 it depends on what `general-purpose` infers from the prompt rather than the harness's defined output formats.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/agents/baseline-architect.md` exists with correct agent frontmatter\\n- [ ] Agent produces output containing `## Component Design` and `## Verification Contracts` sections matching the format consumed by `swarm-task-planner`\\n- [ ] Agent loads or references `swarm-task-planner` output format as a contract\\n- [ ] Agent is registered in `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json`\\n- [ ] `add-new-feature` workflow or language manifest configuration references this agent as the Phase 3 fallback\\n- [ ] At least one end-to-end smoke test: run agent against a SKILL.md change scenario and verify output has Component Design and Verification Contracts sections\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/agents/baseline-architect.md` exits 0\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Read `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` before writing the new agent to extract the exact Component Design and Verification Contract format the consumer expects\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 primary work is authoring the agent prompt to produce the correct output format. The agent infrastructure (plugin.json wiring, frontmatter) is boilerplate. Estimated half a day.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n\\nFunctional intent: PRESENT \u2014 create a harness-agnostic baseline architect agent that produces Component Design and Verification Contract outputs compatible with `swarm-task-planner`.\\n\\n**Available**:\\n- Reference format: `plugins/python-engineering/agents/python-cli-design-spec.md` (language-specific design spec to derive from)\\n- Consumer contract: `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` (reads architect output)\\n- Placement path: `plugins/development-harness/agents/` (where harness agents live)\\n- Artifact conventions: `artifact_register` pattern established in codebase\\n- Observed gap evidence: session 2026-03-30 Phase 3 fell through to general-purpose for SKILL.md change\\n\\n**Missing**: None \u2014 all inputs are present and derivable from the reference agents.\\n\",\"digest\":\"bf0d518ccd375b0d3d5dbec057441f77312f2046d9b79120c9f3c13c269877a3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg59PQ\"}"}